+- `FormAppFormSubmissionScenarioTest` publishes the archive's BPMN and forms via
+  `FormAppArchiveService`, starts through Insight, and submits all ten department
+  arms through `FormService`. Missing required values, dropdown placeholders,
+  missing required table cells, anonymous users, and a named non-assignee are
+  refused with the tasks and process variables unchanged. Historic variables
+  pin the legacy arm-specific field IDs, including `user_assignee_owner_mp2`.
+
+### Supported FormApp submission boundary
+
+`FormAppArchiveService.deploy(InputStream)` supports the FormApp `FormProcess`
+archive only. Publication reads numeric form IDs from `form-models/<name>-<id>.json`
+filenames (not the JSON `referenceId`) and stores an immutable
+`insight-form-mappings.json` alias map alongside `forms/FormApp/<name>.json`
+resources in the same process-engine deployment. BPMN references remain numeric;
+runtime resolution uses the task's process-definition deployment, so publishing
+a later version cannot change a running task's form. Ordinary draft app
+publication does not import these archive forms.
+
+`FormService.getFormData(taskId, processDefinitionId)` exposes the stable form
+key, flattened container fields, required flags, current values, dropdown options,
+and table column definitions. The optional process-definition ID must match the
+task. Only the authenticated Insight assignee can read or submit the task form.
+`submitForm` accepts values by declared editable field ID and validates the entire
+request before one Flowable completion command writes those variables. Required
+values cannot be absent, null, blank, or empty; dropdown choices must use a
+declared non-placeholder option ID (a string or `{id: ...}`); dynamic tables are
+lists of row maps with every required column present and nonempty. Dates use ISO
+dates or offset timestamps, and people use an object with an ID. Arm fields map
+directly to process-variable IDs, preserving the legacy golden spine's payloads.
+
+This slice does not implement start-form submission/variable mapping, general
+Kickstart app import or app-engine/identity metadata, visibility expressions,
+REST-backed options, people-directory lookup, field length/range/regex constraints,
+table cell types/options, attachment/content mapping, PDF rendering, listeners,
+candidate/delegated-task permissions, or general draft-editor form publication.
+Readonly mirrors are exposed from their declared process-variable binding and
+cannot be submitted. Static required flags are enforced regardless of visibility.
+The separate engine-only completion path remains outside this form contract.
+The preflight inventory continues to report static publication gaps; it is not a
+behavioral certification. Follow the repository quality bar (Unit tests and
+Build locally, then the exact-head Jenkins/Sonar PR gates).
+
+Focused form checks:
+
+```bash
+JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS=-Djava.awt.headless=true JAVA_HOME=/path/to/jdk-21 \
+  mvn -o -s /path/to/maven-settings.xml -pl insight-rest -am \
